1
00:06:31,764 --> 00:06:37,764
Are teenage dreams so hard to beat?

2
00:13:03,529 --> 00:13:09,529
Good Vibrations is a music, drama film directed by Lisa Barros D'Sa.

3
00:19:35,294 --> 00:19:41,294
The story of music legend Terri Hooley, a key
figure in Belfast's punk rock scene.

4
00:26:07,058 --> 00:26:13,058
Hooley founded the Good Vibrations store from which a record label sprung,
representing bands such as The Undertones, Rudi and The Outcasts.

5
00:32:38,823 --> 00:32:44,823
Terri Hooley, played by Richard Dormer.

6
00:39:10,588 --> 00:39:16,588
Ruth, played by Jodie Whittaker.

7
00:45:42,352 --> 00:45:48,352
George Hooley, played by Karl Johnson.

8
00:52:14,117 --> 00:52:20,117
Dave Hyndman, played by Michael Colgan.

9
00:58:45,882 --> 00:58:51,882
Davy, played by Liam Cunningham.

10
01:05:17,647 --> 01:05:23,647
Pat, played by Dylan Moran.

11
01:11:49,411 --> 01:11:55,411
Good Vibrations is a 2013 comedy-drama film written by Colin Carberry and Glenn
Patterson and directed by Lisa Barros D'Sa and Glenn Leyburn.

12
01:18:21,176 --> 01:18:27,176
It stars Richard Dormer, Jodie Whittaker, Adrian Dunbar,
Liam Cunningham, Karl Johnson and Dylan Moran.

13
01:24:52,941 --> 01:24:58,941
It is based on the life of Terri Hooley, a record-store owner
instrumental in developing Belfast's punk rock scene.

14
01:31:24,705 --> 01:31:30,705
The film was produced by Chris Martin, with Andrew
Eaton, Bruno Charlesworth and David Holmes.

15
01:37:56,470 --> 01:38:02,470
Holmes also co-wrote the soundtrack score.

16
01:44:28,235 --> 01:44:34,235
The tone is emotional.
